    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2YUwbTNFP92MbconEgCJZPM)_\n\n**Problem:** six messages at startup (Elpaca and `use-package`).\n\n**Changes** (`.org` docs and tangled `.el`, plus `docs/architecture/load-order.org`):\n- `Duplicate item ID queued` for `hl-todo`, `org-autolist`, `elisp-demos`: each was `:ensure t` in two modules. One module installs it, the other is now `:ensure nil` and keeps its own config (`hl-todo`: `sp-org-taskman-extra` installs, `sp-faces` has hooks; `org-autolist`: `sp-org-appearance` installs; `elisp-demos`: `sp-help` installs).\n- `company previously queued as dependency of (company-math company-prescient)`: `company` is now the first form of `sp-completion`; the second declaration in `sp-base-code` is `:ensure nil`.\n- `citar-denote/:init: sp-bibliography is void`: `sp-academic` defined `sp-bibliography`, `sp-bib-notes` and `sp-citar-note` after requiring the modules that read them. It is a late module, so I think Elpaca runs `:init` while the file is still loading. The three `defcustom` forms are now first.\n- `code-review ... emacsql-sqlite-connection is not a class`: `code-review` now has `:after forge` and requires `emacsql-sqlite` in `:init`. Also fixed its `(setq code-review-download-dir ...)` inside `:custom`, which never set the variable.\n- `load-order.org` has a new section with a table of the duplicates and the two module-internal fixes; the dot graph label for `sp-minibuffer` is updated.\n\n**Not tested:** no Emacs here. The company, bibliography and code-review causes are my reading of the code and of Elpaca's behaviour, not confirmed by a run; `code-review` could still fail if the cause is a version mismatch between `emacsql`, `closql` and `code-review` rather than order. A scan of all modules found no other package with two `:ensure` declarations. Bracket balance checked; docs tangle to the `.el` as before.\n\n**Overlap:** #86 edits `sp-academic.org` and `.el` in other places (bibtex and citar options); should merge cleanly.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01PF79fi4scSSid1V5FvNkEF)_",
    "changed_files": 17,
    "closed_at": "2026-10-25T13:39:39Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "OWNER",
            "body": "This is what Claude provided as info:\r\n\r\nI opened [PR #87](https://github.com/siainbuletin/dotfiles/pull/87) (branch 87-fix-package-order) for the six startup messages. It’s separate from #86. I couldn’t run Emacs, so none of it is tested.\r\n\r\nhl-todo, org-autolist, elisp-demos: each was :ensure t in two modules. One module installs it and the other is now :ensure nil and keeps its own config. sp-org-taskman-extra, sp-org-appearance and sp-help install; sp-faces, sp-org-ext and sp-lisp don’t. A scan of every module found no other package declared twice.\r\ncompany: company is now the first form in sp-completion, ahead of company-math and company-prescient. The second declaration in sp-base-code is :ensure nil. I couldn’t see why the first one didn’t already win, so this part is a guess.\r\nsp-bibliography void: sp-academic defined the variable after requiring the modules that read it, and it’s a late module. I think Elpaca runs :init while the file is still loading. The three defcustom forms now come first.\r\ncode-review: it now has :after forge and requires emacsql-sqlite in :init, so the parent class exists before its own class is defined. I also fixed its (setq code-review-download-dir …) inside :custom, which never set the variable. If the real cause is a version mismatch between emacsql, closql and code-review, this won’t fix it. I didn’t find a source that settles it.\r\n\r\nload-order.org has a new section with a table of the duplicates and the two module-internal fixes. Its dot graph label for sp-minibuffer is updated too, and CI builds the SVG.",
